# Keep a polkit authentication agent in the session.
#
# Wayfire's autostart launches a process and does not bring it back if it dies,
# and an agent that is not running is not a degraded session but a broken one:
# with nobody for polkit to ask, every privileged action fails the moment it is
# asked, with no prompt at all. That reads as "permission denied" for joining
# Wi-Fi or setting the timezone and gives no hint why. The agent this image
# used to carry made that concrete by faulting every time it had to draw its
# dialog; see profiles/graphical/packages.list.
#
# So the agent is supervised rather than launched. The pause keeps a binary
# that cannot start at all from spinning.
set -eu

agent=/usr/bin/lxpolkit

while :; do
    "$agent" || true
    sleep 2
done
